A||||8||lowCG||Insurance for modified cars||||5||
Z||000000||lowCG||05-24-2000||10:53 PM||||I have some reservations about even parking my car on the street with a $2000+(parts only) motor swap, $800 suspension,and wheels/tires,etc.<P>Does anyone know of insurance that'll even cover over half of what we've done to our cars?<P>Had my insurance company(Safeco)screw me out of a couple thousand $ here a couple years back,wouldn't like to have it happen again.||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero mistress||05-25-2000||12:03 AM||||The best thing I can tell you to do is to have your car appraised and insure it at appraised value.<P>With an "At Value" insurance policy you will have restrictions on your insurance coverages.  What those specific restrictions are depends on the policy/company.<P>I suggest you appraise the car and then begin your insurance policy shopping.<P>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||05-25-2000||12:17 AM||||My insurance company will not let me state a<BR>"declared value" until the car is 15 years old.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||phillip||05-25-2000||11:26 AM||||look for the corvette forum (just like this one). i've seen it discussed a few times there but i don't remember what companies and details were mentioned.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phoenix||05-25-2000||12:24 PM||||Check with The Great American Insurance Company,  I have one of my cars insured with them on a stated value policy.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||05-25-2000||12:34 PM||||Even with "normal" insurance, always keep receipts for parts and work done. Both my insurance company (State Farm) and the insurance company (American Family) of the driver that totalled by stepson's Fiero will calculate "recent" money spent into the value. They said it's not $ for $, they have some sort of formula they use. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Roy||05-25-2000||02:05 PM||||I'm using progressive for insurance right now, the prices are low. And they allow you to insure up to $4,000 worth of custom parts on your car. So if anything happends my engine swap is covered. Secondly, I use to use American Family Insurance. They allow you to declare the value of your car atleast on my 84 they did. I dunno if you can on 88's. I didn't have my 88 at the time I was using them. But they allowed me to declare the value of my 84 at 8k because of all the custom stuff. Hope this information helps.<P>Roy||||reg||10
Z||000007||Monkeyman||05-25-2000||02:07 PM||||RossT--Shoulda bought an '85 GT.  Then your car would be old enough. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Call Progessive.  The Grape Ape is insured for face value (admittedly not a whole lot right now, but more than the book value).  They told me that, if I need to up the coverage, all I need to do is show proof of any upgrades (pics and receipts) and make a phone call.||||reg||1
Z||000008||lowCG||05-25-2000||11:04 PM||||Wow,thanks,that's alot of good info,from all angles too.<BR>I'll definately sleep better knowing that I can protect my investment.||||reg||1
